      "content": "Traditionalists often argue that modern changes to marriage and family, such as dual breadwinner marriages, single-parent households, and same-sex relationships, undermine the traditional role of husband and wife as reciprocal caregivers, creating an inequitable distribution of labor and care within the home. They often cite a biblical mandate to \"be fruitful and multiply\" (Genesis 1:28) as a justification for the traditional nuclear family. Additionally, some traditionalists point to the alleged decline in family stability, children being raised in single-parent households, and an increase in divorce rates as evidence of the negative consequences of modern changes. They believe this setup is a threat to the well-being of children and the family unit.",
